// STIX 2.1: the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// A threat intelligence bundle on Operation Quiet Invoice, a fictional phishing campaign against a UK building
// society. It holds the threat actor, intrusion set and campaign; the real ATT&CK attack patterns and Rclone tool
// they use; the InvoiceDrop dropper and LedgerRAT implant with their command and control infrastructure; the email,
// files, processes, domain, addresses and network traffic observed on the victim's network; and the indicators,
// sighting, sandbox analysis, courses of action, opinion and TLP:AMBER report around them. Names, domains (example.*)
// and addresses (203.0.113.0/24, AS64500) are reserved for documentation; hashes are illustrative.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The model: its constraints

